          "kind": "text",
          "value": "A startup recorded the daily step counts (in thousands) of 8 users: 8, 17, 15, 19, 21, 25, 23, 35. To spot\nunusually active users, the startup sets a threshold defined as: Threshold = Q3 + 1.5 × IQR. Any user\nwhose step count is above this threshold will be marked as an outlier. How many users will be marked as\noutliers?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "For percentiles, use the nearest-rank method: sort n observations and take the value at rank ceil(n·p) for percentile proportion p."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 4,
      "difficulty": "hard",
